\title{stepcadence: Computes Cadence Metrics from Step Count Data}
\description{
Computes cadence (steps per minute) metrics from minute-level step count data, such as data from the National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey (NHANES), as described in Tudor-Locke et al. (2018) \doi{10.1136/bjsports-2017-097628}. Metrics include peak 1-, 30-, and 60-minute cadence, maximum 5-, 20-, 30-, and 60-minute consecutive cadence, uncensored and censored mean cadence, and time spent in cadence bands and levels, with optional masking of non-wear time.
}
\details{
Start with \code{\link[=summarize_cadence]{summarize_cadence()}}, which computes every metric.  The
individual metrics are available from \code{\link[=compute_daily_steps]{compute_daily_steps()}},
\code{\link[=compute_cadence_peak]{compute_cadence_peak()}}, \code{\link[=compute_cadence_max]{compute_cadence_max()}},
\code{\link[=compute_cadence_mean]{compute_cadence_mean()}}, \code{\link[=compute_cadence_level]{compute_cadence_level()}},
\code{\link[=compute_cadence_minutes_above]{compute_cadence_minutes_above()}}, \code{\link[=compute_cadence_bouts]{compute_cadence_bouts()}},
\code{\link[=compute_cadence_extended_bout]{compute_cadence_extended_bout()}}, and \code{\link[=compute_cadence_bands]{compute_cadence_bands()}}.
\code{\link[=cadence_thresholds]{cadence_thresholds()}} gives age-specific intensity thresholds and
\code{\link[=step_volume_category]{step_volume_category()}} classifies steps/day.

Input is minute-level data with \code{time} and \code{steps} columns, plus
optional \code{wear} and \code{counts} columns.  Use \code{group_cols} (or
\code{\link[dplyr:group_by]{dplyr::group_by()}}) to compute metrics per participant or per day.
}
